    "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.10.26.08.19.32/chromadotnet.local.core.1.5.9.1-preview.4.json#deprecation",
    "alternatePackage": {
      "@id": "https://api.nuget.org/v3/catalog0/data/2026.10.26.08.19.32/chromadotnet.local.core.1.5.9.1-preview.4.json#deprecation/alternatePackage",
      "id": "ChromaDotNet.Local.ChromaDB",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "ChromaDotNet.Local.Core is replaced by ChromaDotNet.Local.ChromaDB, which brings the base ChromaDotNet.Local, and the code stays the same. To download the executable at the first start, as Core alone did, set ChromaDotNetLocalChromaDBDownload to true in the project.",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
  "description": "The code of ChromaDotNet.Local, without the Chroma executables. At the first start it downloads the executable of the platform from the GitHub release of ChromaDB.Local and checks its SHA-256. To work offline, add the ChromaDotNet.Local.Runtime package of each platform, or reference ChromaDotNet.Local, which brings them all. ChromaLocalServer.StartAsync starts Chroma 1.5.9 as a child process on 127.0.0.1, for ChromaDotNet.Client, and stops it with Dispose or when the application ends. Community project, not affiliated with Chroma.",
